# basedverse's settings: a template, with nothing real in it. Copy what you need into a .env (never
# committed; .gitignore keeps it out) and fill it in. Blank means the default. `bin/setup` writes the first
# section into a workroom's .env for you, asking for what it needs.

# -- A workroom's visit (visit/INTEGRATING.md, step 2) ----------------------------------------------------
# visit, the one program a workroom runs, reads these from its environment (each is also a flag: VISIT_PORT is
# --port). A workroom keeps them in its own settings, its .env say, starting from this section, and its launcher
# passes them on. Its database, its sign-in and its engine are inside it: there is no address to give for them.

# The lobby's address, from whoever runs it: wss://<its IP address or DNS name>/
VISIT_LOBBY=
# The office's name in the lobby: 1-24 letters, digits, space, _ . -, starting and ending with a letter or
# digit. In quotes if it has a space ("My Room"), so a shell can load this file too.
VISIT_NAME=
# The sim, as name/version, shown to others, e.g. my-workroom/1.0 (default unknown/0).
VISIT_SIM=
# visit's port for the page (default 7401).
VISIT_PORT=
# The address it answers the page on (default 127.0.0.1: this machine only). 0.0.0.0 only in a container: its
# container's own network, its port never published (engine/SPEC.md 6.1).
VISIT_LISTEN=
# How many visitors the room takes at once, 0-8 (default 3).
VISIT_MAX_VISITORS=
# The page's origins, comma-separated: scheme://host:port as the address bar shows them, e.g.
# http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000. visit refuses any other site's page, token or not.
# Blank lets any page with the token in: name yours.
VISIT_ORIGINS=
# The file the launcher writes a new page token to on every run (mode 0600): the host's token. The token
# itself never goes in a .env: it is new each run.
VISIT_TOKEN_FILE=
# The file the launcher writes a new user token to on every run (mode 0600), for a room on the engine: what the
# workroom's server relays the person with (engine/INTEGRATING.md, step 3). Blank: no user connection is taken.
VISIT_USER_TOKEN_FILE=
# The relays for links, overriding the lobby's: none, default (iroh's public ones), or comma-separated
# URLs (default: the ones the lobby names).
VISIT_RELAYS=
# Where the workroom keeps everything: its database, its state file, friends' landscapes, the engine's browser
# profile. A secret (it holds the office's key and the database's passwords, readable by you only): the user's
# own, outside any repository, written out in full (no ~). Blank: the user's data folder, basedverse/<the
# office's name as a folder> (for "My Room": ~/.local/share/basedverse/my-room on Linux, ~/Library/Application
# Support/basedverse/my-room on macOS, %LOCALAPPDATA%\basedverse\my-room on Windows). bin/setup writes it here
# once, so a renamed office keeps its data.
VISIT_DATA_DIR=
# Where visit keeps what outlasts a run: whether the office went offline (the panel's Go offline, or
# leaveLobby()), so a restart stays offline; the office's key, so it is the same office to the friends who made
# it their guest; its door and its guests. A secret. Blank: state.json in VISIT_DATA_DIR.
VISIT_STATE_FILE=
# Where visit keeps friends' landscapes (the parts of their rooms that never change: sent once) and their plots
# to draw while they are away. Blank: landscapes/ in VISIT_DATA_DIR.
VISIT_CACHE_DIR=
# Exit after this many seconds with no page connected (default 0: never).
VISIT_IDLE_EXIT=
# Not visit's but its launcher's: where visit is (bin/setup puts it in visit/client/bin/ and writes its path
# here). Blank: visit on the PATH.
VISIT_PATH=

# -- A workroom's sign-in (auth/INTEGRATING.md) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Served by visit itself when AUTH_TOKEN_FILE is given (each is also a flag: AUTH_PORT is --auth-port). The
# launcher passes them on with the rest; the workroom's server gets AUTH_PORT and AUTH_TOKEN_FILE too.

# The file the launcher writes a new service token to on every run (mode 0600), for visit and the workroom's
# server. The token itself never goes in a .env. Blank: no sign-in API.
AUTH_TOKEN_FILE=
# The sign-in API's port (default 7403).
AUTH_PORT=
# Its address (default 127.0.0.1). 0.0.0.0 only in a container, as VISIT_LISTEN.
AUTH_LISTEN=
# A session ends after this long unused, and this long in all: a number and s, m, h or d (default 7d and 30d).
AUTH_IDLE=
AUTH_MAX_AGE=

# -- A workroom's engine (engine/INTEGRATING.md) ------------------------------------------------------------
# The room's server page, hosted by visit itself in the headless Chrome inside it, when ENGINE_ROOM_URL is given
# (each is also a flag: ENGINE_PORT is --engine-port).

# The room's server page, on the workroom's server: http://127.0.0.1:3001/room/server, say (?role=host if one
# page serves both roles). Its origin goes in VISIT_ORIGINS too. Blank: no engine.
ENGINE_ROOM_URL=
# The engine's /health, on VISIT_LISTEN's address (default 7405).
ENGINE_PORT=
# Frames a second the room gets with nobody there, 1-60 (default 10).
ENGINE_TICK_IDLE=
# MiB the engine's browser may hold before it is started again (default 1024).
ENGINE_MEMORY_MAX=
# The room page's window, WIDTHxHEIGHT: what its camera and canvas are told; nothing is drawn (default 1280x720).
ENGINE_WINDOW=
# The engine's log: error, warn, info or debug (default info). Its page's console goes there.
ENGINE_LOG=

# -- Running the lobby (lobby/README.md, "Put it on a server") -------------------------------------------
# The server bin/deploy-lobby deploys to (user@host, e.g. ubuntu@203.0.113.5) and its ssh key file, if
# ssh needs one. It fills these in itself on the first deploy.
LOBBY_DEPLOY=
LOBBY_DEPLOY_KEY=
# The directory it deploys into on the server (default basedverse-lobby), for a server set up
# under another name.
LOBBY_DEPLOY_DIR=
# The address of the lobby it last deployed (it writes it; bin/setup offers it).
LOBBY_DEPLOY_URL=
